---@field tools? github.agent_automations.CreateRepoAutomationRequestToolsList The tools available to the automation.
---@field enabled? boolean Whether the automation should be created enabled. Defaults to true when omitted.
---@field type? github.agent_automations.CreateRepoAutomationRequestType|string The type of automation, fixed at creation. `personal` keeps it private to its creator and its runs act as that user. `shared` makes it belong to the repository, visible to anyone with read access to the repository and maintainable by anyone with write access to the repository, and its runs act as the Copilot app rather than as a person. `shared` is rejected when repository ownership is not available for the repository. Supported values: `personal`, `shared`. Defaults to `personal`.
---@field require_actor_write_permission? boolean When true, event-triggered runs require the event actor to have repo write permission, even when the org's allow_read_access_triggers policy is enabled. When policy validation is enabled, explicitly setting false returns 422 if effective organization or repository policy disallows read-access triggers. If omitted, defaults to false when policy permits read-access triggers, otherwise true. The actor requirement does not apply to interval-scheduled runs, which always run as the automation owner.
---@field continuous_history? boolean When true, runs of this automation build on the session history of its previous runs, and runs of the same automation are serialized. Not tracked in revision history. Defaults to false.

---The reasoning effort to use for sessions triggered by this automation. Omit or leave empty to use the model's default.
